  Do not disable SSL verification based on a hostname heuristic.

  is_staging() matches public, production-capable hosts. .dev is a real
  public TLD, and .cloudwaysapps.com, .kinsta.cloud, .wpengine.com and
  .sg-host.com are used for live stores. On any such site
  get_http_request_args() sets sslverify => false and
  reject_unsafe_urls => false for every license request, so the license
  key and activation response travel over an unverified TLS channel and
  become MITM-modifiable.

  Gate the relaxed transport on an explicit local-only signal instead, for
  example WP_ENVIRONMENT_TYPE of local/development, or
  wp_get_environment_type(), plus a filter the merchant must opt into.


  🔒️ Proposed restriction of the relaxed transport

   		private function get_http_request_args( $custom_args = array() ) {
   
   			$defaults = array(
   				'timeout' => 15,
   			);
   
  -			// Disable SSL verification and safe URLs for local/staging environments only.
  -			if ( $this->is_staging() ) {
  +			// Only relax transport security on an explicitly declared local/development site.
  +			$environment = function_exists( 'wp_get_environment_type' ) ? wp_get_environment_type() : 'production';
  +
  +			if ( in_array( $environment, array( 'local', 'development' ), true ) ) {
   				$defaults['reject_unsafe_urls'] = false;
   				$defaults['sslverify']          = false;
   			}
   
   			return wp_parse_args( $custom_args, $defaults );
