  Handle a single-token street line.

  explode(' ', $line, 2) produces one element for a line with no space.
  The count($parts) === 2 guard then skips the street-number extraction,
  so an address_1 of "123" returns streetNumber empty and streetName
  "123". Moneris receives a house number as the street name. Accept a
  digit-only single token as the street number.






  ♻️ Proposed adjustment

           $parts = explode(' ', $line, 2);
   
           if (count($parts) === 2 && preg_match('/[0-9]/', $parts[0])) {
               $result['streetNumber'] = $parts[0];
               $result['streetName']   = trim($parts[1]);
  +        } elseif (1 === count($parts) && preg_match('/^[0-9]+[A-Za-z]?$/', $parts[0])) {
  +            $result['streetNumber'] = $parts[0];
  +            $result['streetName']   = '';
           }


