  Configure the WordPress sniff properties.

  rule ref="WordPress" enables
  WordPress.NamingConventions.PrefixAllGlobals and WordPress.WP.I18n.
  Both need properties before they produce useful output. Without a
  prefixes value, the prefix sniff reports every global function and class
  in this plugin as an error. Without a text_domain value, the i18n sniff
  cannot detect a wrong domain, which is the exact defect fixed in
  GatewayResponseMessageHelper.php in this same change.

  The repository guideline requires a PHPCS run after every PHP edit, so the
  ruleset must be usable as configured.

  As per coding guidelines: "After modifying any PHP file, immediately run
  PHPCS on that file and fix the reported issues".






  ♻️ Proposed configuration

  -	<rule ref="WordPress"/>
  +	<rule ref="WordPress"/>
  +
  +	<rule ref="WordPress.NamingConventions.PrefixAllGlobals">
  +		<properties>
  +			<property name="prefixes" type="array">
  +				<element value="wpheka"/>
  +				<element value="WPHEKA"/>
  +				<element value="woocommerce_gateway_moneris_pro"/>
  +				<element value="Woocommerce_Gateway_Moneris_Pro"/>
  +			</property>
  +		</properties>
  +	</rule>
  +
  +	<rule ref="WordPress.WP.I18n">
  +		<properties>
  +			<property name="text_domain" type="array">
  +				<element value="wpheka-gateway-moneris-pro"/>
  +			</property>
  +		</properties>
  +	</rule>


