  Guard the checksum target before reading it.

  file_get_contents($file) emits a PHP warning when $file does not exist
  or is unreadable. The warning reaches the site error log and, on
  misconfigured hosts, the page output. Add an is_readable() check before
  the read.






  🛡️ Proposed guard

  -    $content = file_get_contents($file);
  -    if ($content === false) {
  +    if (!is_string($file) || '' === $file || !is_readable($file)) {
  +        return false;
  +    }
  +
  +    $content = file_get_contents($file);
  +    if ($content === false) {
           return false;
       }


